<Base locale="en" slug="cases/ambiguous-operation" title="The action was sent, but the outcome is unknown" description="A teaching scenario for controlled recovery from an ambiguous operation." kicker="Case · ambiguous operation" lede="The risk is not only a mistake. It is retrying an action when nobody knows whether it already had an external effect." sources="TENIR teaching scenario · no real banking transaction demonstrated">
  <p class="banner"><strong>Teaching scenario.</strong> No real banking settlement is demonstrated.</p>
  <ol class="case-steps"><li><strong>Prepare</strong><span>An operation is built with amount, beneficiary and identifier.</span></li><li><strong>Authorize</strong><span>The request passes identity and scope checks.</span></li><li><strong>Evaluate</strong><span>The boundary re-evaluates the context at execution time.</span></li><li><strong>Record UNKNOWN</strong><span>The provider does not clearly confirm dispatch or effect.</span></li><li><strong>HOLD</strong><span>Automatic retry is suspended to avoid a duplicate.</span></li><li><strong>Reconcile</strong><span>External evidence or a bounded human decision is sought.</span></li><li><strong>Close</strong><span>The next step is recorded with facts, unknowns and an owner.</span></li></ol>
  <section class="decision-sheet"><h2>Operational decision sheet</h2><dl><dt>Available facts</dt><dd>Authorization recorded, request sent, provider response absent or incomplete.</dd><dt>Unknowns</dt><dd>Did the external effect happen? Was the same identifier accepted?</dd><dt>Actors</dt><dd>Operations, finance, provider, process owner, audit.</dd><dt>Immediate decision</dt><dd>Keep HOLD; do not retry blindly.</dd><dt>Evidence to request</dt><dd>Correlated provider reference, settlement state, timestamp and operation identity.</dd><dt>Next action</dt><dd>Reconcile, then resume or cancel within a written scope.</dd><dt>Designated owner</dt><dd>To be named by the organization; the demonstration does not choose one.</dd></dl></section>
</Base>
